       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A confirmation without a clinical rationale isn't enough for me to enter amlodipine 50 mg daily. That's five times the maximum labeled dose of 10 mg. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, I can't think of an indication that justifies it, and the risk of severe hypotension and shock is high.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Change the dose.** Give me 5 mg or 10 mg and I'll enter it immediately.\n- **Add a second agent.** If 10 mg isn't controlling blood pressure, I can enter a different antihypertensive, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic, at a dose you specify.\n- **Discuss it with pharmacy or an attending.** If you think there's an unusual reason for this dose, they can review it first. You can also enter it yourself through the normal override process.\n\nIf I've misunderstood something, for example if the intended dose or drug was different, tell me and I'll enter the corrected order."
      }
